---
type: fix-verification
title: Accepted stream keeps the caller's read timeout
description: The CielAiRouter retry deadline clipped the socket timeout and left it on the accepted response, cutting long streams at 60 seconds; accepted responses now get the caller's timeout back.
tags: [cielairouter, timeout, responses, transient-retry]
timestamp: 2026-10-21
status: source-verified
---

# Defect

bounded_timeout clips each opener socket timeout to the transient-retry
deadline (60 seconds by default) so a stalled open cannot outlive it. The
clipped value stayed on the socket after HTTP 200 acceptance, so a native
Responses stream that was still generating after 60 seconds (even with a
configured request timeout of 120 seconds or more) ended with
UpstreamStreamReadError -> HTTP 502 upstream_stream_truncated
"TimeoutError: timed out; attempts=1". The checkpoint-recovery reopen in
provider_responses_passthrough had the same leak.

# Change

- TransientRetryBudget records the caller's requested timeout inside
  bounded_timeout (requested_timeout).
- release_read_timeout puts it back on the accepted response socket. _execute
  calls it for every accepted response; the one-shot checkpoint reopen calls
  it explicitly. Invalid requested values keep the clipped bound; None restores
  blocking reads, exactly as the unscoped path.
- Acceptance is unchanged: a stalled open is still bounded by the deadline
  (test_stalled_loopback_headers_hit_bounded_socket_timeout_without_replay).

# Verification

tests/test_transient_retry_read_timeout.py uses a real loopback server whose
SSE stream completes 0.3 seconds after acceptance with a 0.1 second retry
deadline and a 1 second caller timeout:

- Without the change: the production ProviderResponsesPassthrough raised
  "Upstream provider 'cielairouter' response stream was truncated
  (TimeoutError: timed out; model=fixture-model; attempts=1)", the
  screenshot's message.
- With the change: full body forwarded, one upstream request, accepted socket
  timeout 1.0, generic provider unchanged.

evidence/focused-tests.txt: 419 exact-file tests OK (42 existing retired
architecture skips), covering transient retry, preamble, deadline,
integration, upstream retry, Responses passthrough, compaction and
architecture budgets. Ruff and diff whitespace checks passed.

# Not established

The screenshot's router (127.0.0.1:9179) was not present on this host, so that
specific incident is matched by signature only. The separate
"semantic context compaction failed: truncated_summary" errors in the 9512
session are a different mechanism: the summary request returned with a
truncation stop reason after about 39 seconds; the exact stop reason is not
logged. That is not changed here. No commit, publish or live session restart
was performed.
